The thermodynamic core of this package (winton_seaice_model.py: the implicit surface-temperature solve, the
layer enthalpies, the thickness update with surface and basal melt, snowfall, flooding and layer
re-equalisation) is a port to JAX of the MITgcm package pkg/thsice, routines THSICE_SOLVE4TEMP
(thsice_solve4temp.F) and THSICE_CALC_THICKN (thsice_calc_thickn.F), and reproduces those two routines to machine precision for full ice cover
(tests/reference/thsice); the sub-grid fraction closure and the frazil path are this package's own. MITgcm is distributed under the MIT License:

