The scheme is Winton (2000), J. Atmos. Oceanic Technol. 17, 525-531. The sub-grid lead closure follows
Hibler (1979), J. Phys. Oceanogr. 9, 815-846, and is not part of thsice. The bulk surface fluxes over ice use
the coefficients of SPEEDY / JCM (jax-gcm). The optional transport (ice_transport.py) is original code
following published practice: thickness diffusion as in Ferreira, Marshall and Rose (2011), J. Climate 24,
992-1012; advection by the surface ocean current as in the GENIE (Edwards and Marsh 2005, Clim. Dyn. 24,
415-433) and Bern3D models; and a no-convergence-into-compact-ice rule that simplifies the cavitating-fluid
rheology of Flato and Hibler (1992), J. Phys. Oceanogr. 22, 626-651.
